# Task 7 — repair legacy-readiness descendant authentication

## Confirmed failure and root cause

The exact provider-free schema-v3 manifest build reproducibly fails before
writing `manifest.json` with `legacy readiness source identity differs from
source root`. The legacy schema-v1 readiness is canonical and authenticated but
was created before the model-authored policy extraction and rounded-stop safety
fix. The final parity attestation is specifically the authenticated bridge from
a later corrected reference commit to the current clean source. The manifest
builder incorrectly requires the legacy source identity itself to equal the
current source, then later also requires parity's final identity to equal that
legacy identity. That rejects every legitimate descendant migration.

## Boundaries

- Worktree: `C:/Projects/trading_bot/RS-momentum-EMA-trading-bot/.worktrees/pit-optimizer-implementation`.
- Required clean base HEAD: `b62411b2c84cfe690406aa1af48f51bcae1b9c66`.
