  adjustment is strictly required.
- Do not add or modify tests/docs/manifests. Do not touch the rounded-stop clamp.
- Do not create/overwrite optimizer manifest/readiness/parity artifacts, call a
  provider/network/pricing service, start Docker, open hidden data, grant,
  evaluate a candidate, run replay, push, or merge.
- Preserve every existing PIT bundle/baseline/effective-policy/fold/parity
  equality gate and schema-v3 calls/tokens/retries/apply/USD contracts.

## Required correction

1. Keep canonical legacy-readiness authentication through
   `_authenticated_readiness` and its retained source/policy/data identities.
2. Require the legacy readiness source head and the parity reference source head
   to be valid, distinct local Git commits, with the legacy source an ancestor
   of the parity reference source.
3. Require the parity reference source to be an ancestor of the parity final
   source/current source (the normal verifier already proves this; recheck at
   manifest sealing for defense in depth).
4. Require parity `final_source_head` and
   `final_source_fingerprint_sha256` to equal the current clean source identity.
5. Stop requiring legacy readiness source head/fingerprint to equal current
   source. Still require its fingerprint to be a valid retained digest through
   existing readiness validation.
6. In the later parity identity-graph check, compare parity's final identity to
   the actual current source, while retaining exact PIT bundle, baseline,
   effective-policy, and discovery-fold-manifest equality.
7. Fail closed on missing/divergent/non-ancestor commits or any Git ancestry
   verification error. Do not weaken create-only output behavior.

